   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Random Letter Swap Ping-Pong\n\nLetters swap out in a random order and, after a hold, swap back in another random-feeling wave (ping-pong).\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 6 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A word should roll out and then roll back, like a hover-in and hover-out on a button or link.\n- The letters should swap in a random order.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The letters should turn into different letters or words: use text-rotate, type-fossil or kinetic-type-swap.\n- A one-time entrance is enough: use per-character-rise or vertical-cut-reveal.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Letter swap\"\n- font_size (number, 24-400): Font size, default 150\n- color (color): Color, default \"#111111\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- reverse (boolean): Reverse, default true\n- stagger (number, 0-0.3): Stagger, default 0.02\n- spring_duration (number, 0.2-2): Spring duration, default 0.8\n- bounce (number, 0-0.8): Bounce, default 0.25\n- swaps (number, 1-8): Cycles, default 2\n- first_swap (number, 0-4): First swap, default 0.4\n- interval (number, 0.6-5): Interval, default 2.2\n- hold (number, 0.2-4): Hold, default 1.0\n\nSource: https://github.com/danielpetho/fancy. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
